# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the LEO Study application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version 1.3.1 to project dependencies
- Used npm to install the package

### 2. Modified Files

#### src/App.tsx
- Added import statement for SpeedInsights component from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the main App component's return statement, just before the closing `</div>` tag
- This placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all pages and routes in the React application

#### package.json
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` dependency

#### package-lock.json
- Updated with new dependency information for Speed Insights package

## Implementation Details

This is a React + Vite application, so I followed the Vercel Speed Insights guide for React applications:
- Imported the `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Placed the component in the main App component to ensure tracking across all routes

The implementation is minimal and non-intrusive, following React best practices. The component will automatically:
- Track real user performance metrics (Core Web Vitals)
- Send data to Vercel's Speed Insights dashboard
- Only activate when deployed to Vercel (no impact in local development)

## Testing

1. ✅ Build verification - Project builds successfully with no errors
2. ✅ Linter check - No new linting errors introduced by the changes
3. ✅ Import verification - SpeedInsights component properly imported and typed

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. The tracking script will be available at `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js`
3. Performance data will start appearing in the Speed Insights dashboard after users visit the site
4. Metrics will include LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, and INP

The implementation preserves all existing functionality and code structure while adding comprehensive performance monitoring capabilities.
